# Delete unfinished motivation jobs

If a job never wrote `output/{slug}-motivation.mp4`, delete the **whole job folder**. Same if user/agent rejects it (horrible clips, remake, do not ship).

## Delete

- No `output/*.mp4` after a failed, aborted, or abandoned run
- Rendered mp4 but visuals/speech failed ship (REMAKE / horrible clips)

```
# ❌ BAD — leftover half-jobs sit next to shipped work
downloads/motivational/2026-09-14/audi-r8-tate
downloads/motivational/2026-09-14/bentley-continental-tate
downloads/motivational/2026-09-14/lamborghini-huracan-tate-v2
downloads/motivational/2026-09-14/audi-r8-tate-v2   # rendered, horrible clips

# ✅ GOOD — only finished keepers remain
downloads/motivational/2026-09-14/audi-r8-tate-v3
downloads/motivational/2026-09-14/lamborghini-huracan-tate
```

```powershell
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force downloads\motivational\<date>\<slug>
. .\scripts\load_agent_path.ps1; python scripts/content_reuse.py rebuild
```

If that slug auto-registered:

```powershell
python scripts/production_library_cli.py delete --video-id <id>
```

## Do not delete

- Shipped keepers with a good `output/*.mp4`
- `downloads/production_library/` unless user rejects that video
- `broll-pool/`, `speech-pool/`, date folders themselves
- A job still rendering
